speechtext:
For the information of my hon. friend, and also for the information of the hon. member for Joliette-L'Assomption-Mont-calm (Mr. Pigeon), I will say that I am also in favour of a lottery.
Mr. Chevrier declared in the house that the file on lotteries was quite voluminous and that it was being considered. We trust that a practical agreement will be reached and that a practical solution will be found.
[Text}

Mr. Chairman, I should just like to ask the minister if she will clarify the point, because actually the resolution on the order paper now states, among other things:
-for the payment of an additional pension of ten dollars a month to all persons to whom a pension may be paid under the Old Age Security Act;
I ask the minister simply whether she is going through with this resolution. Does she contemplate amending it?
